Description: Reopen a tab in its container in the window of the tab it replaces.
 The tab which reopens a page assigned to a container is created in the window which had the focus last, at the
 index of the tab it replaces in that tab's own window, and the tab it replaces is removed at once. When Firefox opens
 a link from another application in a new window while another window has the focus, as during a start which restores
 the session, the page opens as a tab of that other window, and the link's window closes with its only tab. When the
 tab it replaces stays, it is the opener of the new tab, and Firefox refuses to create a tab in another window than
 its opener's, so the page does not open at all.
 .
 The new tab is now created in the window of the tab it replaces, and that tab is removed only once the new one
 exists, so that the window does not close before. When the new tab cannot be created, the tab stays.
Author: Mitar
Bug: https://github.com/mozilla/multi-account-containers/issues/2000
Forwarded: https://github.com/mozilla/multi-account-containers/pull/2957
Last-Update: 2026-11-09
